user information is stored in /etc/passwd
password information is stored in /etc/shadow
group information is stored in /etc/group
when creating or editing users or groups, /etc/login.defs provides default configuration information such as UID or password policy 


SuperUser access:
sudo permissions are defined in /etc/sudoers or /etc/sudoers.d/*
in the file:
username ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL
%groupname ALL=(ALL) ALL
username ALL=(ALL) ALL, !/sbin/useradd




